  "444 A1A2 · Tick Swing Fanfare": "A Haar saw read from the middle of its cycle against a tick of noise; each note's envelope pushes the wavelet towards Daubechies 8, by an amount the LFO swings, and LFO 2 sweeps the scale filter.",
  "445 A1B1 · Hollow Harp": "Only the odd scales, hollow as a clarinet against a bright Haar ping; the wavelet morphs towards Daubechies 20.",
  "446 A1A2 · Snap Beam Pluck": "A pure sine against a tick of noise an octave above; the filtered part of the cycle is swept along it, and LFO 2 changes how far each note's envelope opens the filter.",
  "449 A1A2 · Resonance Strum": "A hollow square against a breath chiff an octave below; the scale cutoff breathes, and the resonance of the scale filter pulses.",
  "451 A1A2 · Click Morph": "A glassy square against a tick of noise; LFO 2 drifts the wavelet towards Daubechies 8.",
  "452 A1A2 · Bloom Pluck": "A soft triangle against a narrow pulse shifted inside its cycle an octave below; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms.",
