  "457 A1B1 · Moon Pick": "A pure sine against scales that die from the top, like a pluck; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms.",
  "459 A1A2 · Swell Harp": "A pure sine against a gritty Haar saw a fifth above; the scale cutoff breathes.",
  "461 A1A2B1 · Timber & Breath": "Low mirrored atoms against a Haar saw read from the middle of its cycle, slightly detuned, and a veil of band-passed noise; each note's envelope pushes the wavelet towards Daubechies 20, by an amount the LFO swings, and LFO 2 widens and narrows the filtered window.",
  "462 A1B1 · Milk Lung Strum": "A soft triangle against random atoms that glitter an octave above; the scale cutoff breathes, and each note opens its filter on its own envelope.",
  "464 A1B1 · Mirage Pick": "Ramp atoms that open like a horn against a Haar saw read from the middle of its cycle an octave below; the wavelet morphs towards Daubechies 20.",
  "469 A1B1 · Swell Chimes": "A nasal pulse against a ringing bell of single atoms; the scale cutoff breathes.",
  "470 A1A2B1 · Atom Mallets": "An organ made of single wavelet atoms against a Haar saw read from the middle of its cycle an octave above, and a quick filtered pluck; the resonance of the scale filter pulses, and LFO 2 pulls the even scales in and out.",
  "471 A1A2B1 · Brass & Slate": "Ramp atoms that open like a horn against a gritty Haar saw an octave above, and a sine that dives in pitch an octave above; each note's envelope pushes the wavelet towards Haar, by an amount the LFO swings.",
  "472 A1B1 · Ripple Bars": "An organ made of single wavelet atoms against a glassy square, slightly detuned; the resonance of the scale filter pulses.",
  "473 A1A2B1 · Chiff & Reed": "A nasal pulse against a breath chiff an octave above, and random atoms that glitter, slightly detuned; the scale cutoff breathes.",
  "475 A1B1 · Thorn Bells": "Wavelet drawbars like an organ against a quick filtered pluck an octave below; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms, and LFO 2 swells the resonance.",
  "478 A1B1 · Surge of Ice": "An organ made of single wavelet atoms against a glassy square, slightly detuned; LFO 2 changes how far each note's envelope opens the filter.",
  "479 A1A2 · Fold Shapeshift Bells": "A nasal pulse against a narrow pulse shifted inside its cycle an octave below; the wavelet morphs towards Daubechies 8, and LFO 2 sweeps the scale filter.",
  "481 A1B1 · Chalk Wah Bars": "An organ made of single wavelet atoms against a jagged Haar triangle an octave below; the resonance of the scale filter pulses.",
  "482 A1B1 · Oboe & Temple": "A nasal pulse against a ringing bell of single atoms; the scale cutoff breathes, and LFO 2 thins and thickens the atoms (sparsity).",
